<title>UK: UK M4 grows provisional 11.3 pct in year to Feb.</title>
<headline>UK M4 grows provisional 11.3 pct in year to Feb.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England published the following data on UK monetary aggregates for February -</p>
<p>    MONEY SUPPLY				     FEB	 JAN mth *</p>
<p>    M4 in month	  (adjusted)		1.4	  1.6</p>
<p>	 in year to date (adjusted)		11.3	 9.8</p>
<p>    M4 in month	  (unadjusted)	    1.6	  0.6</p>
<p>	 in year to date (unadjusted)	    11.3	 9.9</p>
<p>Adjusted lending by banks, building</p>
<p>    societies in billions of stg		 8.2	 n/a</p>
<p>NOTE - consensus forecasts M4 10.1 pct yr/yr, M4 lending +5.6 billion stg. * Previously published final figures for January</p>
<p>    Three-month annual M4 rate (adj)	   11.7	n/a</p>
<p>    Six-month annual M4 rate   (adj)	   12.5	n/a</p>
<p>-- LONDON NEWSROOM ++44 171 542 7708</p>
</text>
